    "interpretation": "A->B isolates the quantifier: whether a metric requires every document a multi-hop question needs, or accepts any one of them. B->C isolates granularity: whether retrieving the document is treated as retrieving the evidence. On a single-hop dataset A and B coincide by definition, so the whole gap is granularity. On a dataset whose documents are only one or two chunks long the granularity step is necessarily small, because retrieving the document nearly guarantees retrieving the span."
